# Lesson 26: Integration Activities — Securing an Organisation's Networked Information System

> ACTIVITY:
  **Context.** A microfinance branch (12 staff PCs, a server, Wi-Fi for staff, a customer portal, remote auditors in Douala) suffered a data leak of customer records and several typing errors in loan amounts. The board asks your team to secure the information system and its data.
  **Task (groups of 3–4, 2 periods).**
  1. **Intranet/extranet design** (Lesson 21): define what stays on the intranet (core banking, HR, documents) and what the extranet offers customers and auditors; specify technologies, authentication and DMZ/reverse-proxy placement.
  2. **VPN** (Lesson 22): design and – on the lab VM/router – configure a remote-access VPN for the auditors with certificate-based (digitally signed) authentication and firewall rules exposing only the VPN port; demonstrate an encrypted tunnel and a revoked certificate being rejected.
  3. **Security measures** (Lesson 23): produce a CIA threat table for the branch and a defence-in-depth plan: accounts and password policy, MFA, firewall/VLAN segmentation, security protocols (HTTPS/TLS on the portal, WPA3, SSH), encryption, signatures for loan documents, updates, backups, logging, physical controls, training.
  4. **Data protection & access control** (Lesson 24): implement on the lab server/PC an encrypted volume/archive for customer files, groups and NTFS/Linux permissions matching an RBAC matrix (Teller, Loan officer, Manager, Auditor, IT), and list the further access-control methods (session, physical, monitoring, disposal) and the legal obligations under Law 2024/017.
  5. **Validation & verification** (Lesson 25): configure a loan-entry spreadsheet/form with at least six validation rules and a double-entry check for amounts and account numbers; test with dirty data and report.
  6. **Report and present** (8 min): a security plan document (diagram of intranet/extranet/VPN/DMZ, threat table, RBAC matrix, validation table, evidence screenshots) and a live demonstration of the VPN, permissions and validation.
  **Criteria.** Coherent intranet/extranet architecture; working, correctly firewalled certificate-based VPN; comprehensive, prioritised security measures mapped to CIA; correct encryption and permissions implementation with legal awareness; effective validation/verification design; quality of report and demonstration.

## Rubric

| Criterion | 4 – Excellent | 3 – Good | 2 – Developing | 1 – Beginning |
| Intranet/extranet design | Clear separation, technologies, DMZ/authentication specified | Minor gaps | Vague | Missing |
| VPN implementation | Works; certificates; firewall exposes only VPN; revocation shown | Works with minor issues | Partially configured | Not working |
| Security measures | Complete defence-in-depth mapped to CIA and prioritised | Mostly complete | Generic list | Few/none |
| Data protection & access control | Encryption + RBAC permissions implemented and tested; legal obligations cited | Implemented | Partial | Absent |
| Validation & verification | ≥ 6 rules + double entry tested with evidence | Rules implemented | Few rules | None |
| Report & demonstration | Professional, evidenced, clear | Clear | Basic | Weak |

---
